# "If this spell was cast from a graveyard": a copy of a spell is not cast (CR 707.10), so the copy of a flashed-back
# Esper Origins, made by Lutri flashed in with it on the stack, surveils 2 and gains 2 life but is neither exiled nor put
# onto the battlefield - a copy has no card to put there (CR 707.10a, 111.7 do not apply: it simply does nothing more)
# and ceases to exist as it leaves the stack (CR 704.5e). The original, cast from the graveyard, then surveils 2, gains 2
# and becomes the one Summon: Esper Maduin, whose chapter I reveals Llanowar Elves into Bot1's hand.
# Life: 20 + 2 (turn 1, from hand) + 2 (copy) + 2 (original) = 26. Each surveil bins both cards it looks at, so the
# second surveil sees fresh cards: the copy bins Forest and Island, the original Swamp and Plains (with the
# sacrificed Black Lotus, five cards in the graveyard).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Esper Origins
Lutri, the Spellchaser
Forest
Forest
Island
Swamp
Plains
Llanowar Elves
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

